TITLE: Atomic State Updates with Ref.update in Effect-TS
DESCRIPTION: Demonstrates the correct way to manage shared mutable state concurrently using `Ref.make`, `Ref.update`, and `Ref.get` in Effect-TS. All operations on `Ref` are atomic, ensuring data integrity. This example simulates 1000 concurrent fibers incrementing a counter.

SOURCE: https://github.com/pauljphilp/effectpatterns/blob/main/content/published/manage-shared-state-with-ref.mdx

LANGUAGE: typescript
